<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hyrcania</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hyrcania was a historical region south-east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a>, in the modern Iranian provinces of Golestan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mazandaran">Mazandaran</a> and parts of Turkmenistan. A fertile, forested province of the Achaemenid, Seleucid and Parthian empires, it bordered the steppe of nomadic peoples such as the Dahae. Its name survives in that of the city and plain of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorgan">Gorgan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hyrcania.jpg" alt="Hyrcania" width="320" height="154" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Robert Shepherd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Achaemenid_Empire.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
